<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Advance (250)</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>advance admin &lt;player&gt; &lt;level&gt;
advance ply &lt;player&gt; &lt;level&gt;
</pre>
<p>Examples:
</p>
<pre>advance admin Gnort 210
advance ply Gnort 25
</pre>
<p>Sets the level of a player who is online.
</p><p><b>advance admin</b> gives an immortal level, from 200 to 255. It promotes 
or demotes, with a fitting message to the player, but you can't touch 
someone of a higher level than yours. Their experience is reset to 0, and 
they are no longer hungry or thirsty.
</p><p><b>advance ply</b> sets a mortal's level and gives them the experience that 
level needs; you are shown their experience before and after. It only 
works on mortals: to make an immortal mortal again, the character must be 
deleted and made anew.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Set</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Level</a>
</pre>




</div>